WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:15.130
Wendy was brought up to the deck of the Jolly Roger.

2
00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:20.189
The boys were lined up in their chains trying to look brave.

3
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:25.345
When she saw the pirates preparing the plank, she was filled with hate.

4
00:00:25.346 --> 00:00:29.339
She hated Hook and she hated the pirates.

5
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:35.012
Boys might think pirates exciting, but Wendy did not.

6
00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:39.679
She especially hated that the ship had not been cleaned for years.

7
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.529
Not one window was without a layer of grime.

8
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:50.346
In fact, while she was below, she wrote "Dirty Pig" on a window with her finger.

9
00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:55.772
She also hated that it was nighttime and no one was in bed.

10
00:00:55.773 --> 00:01:01.129
But when the boys gathered around her, all these thoughts melted away.

11
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:08.731
"So, my beauty," said Hook, "soon you will see your children walk the plank."

12
00:01:08.732 --> 00:01:14.985
Hook's lace collar was dirty, and when he saw Wendy staring, he tried to hide it.

13
00:01:14.986 --> 00:01:20.161
"Are the children going to die?" she asked scornfully.

14
00:01:20.162 --> 00:01:24.602
Her voice made it clear how she despised Hook for his plan.

15
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:33.421
"They are!" he shouted. "Silence! Listen to a mother's last words to her children."

16
00:01:33.422 --> 00:01:37.611
Wendy stood tall and faced everyone proudly.

17
00:01:37.612 --> 00:01:41.803
"These are my last words, dear boys," she said.

18
00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:45.130
"I feel that your real mothers would say this:

19
00:01:45.131 --> 00:01:49.412
We hope our sons die like gentlemen."

20
00:01:49.413 --> 00:01:57.849
Hook shuddered. Even the pirates were awed, for Wendy's words were the kind that inspired bravery.

21
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.040
Tootles cried out, "I am going to do what my mother wishes.

22
00:02:03.041 --> 00:02:06.408
What are you going to do, Slightly?"

23
00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:12.841
"What my mother wishes," said Slightly. "What are you going to do, Nibs?"

24
00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:18.840
Nibs answered the same way, and so did the other boys until Hook interrupted.

25
00:02:18.841 --> 00:02:24.072
"Tie her up to the mast!" he shouted cruelly.

26
00:02:24.073 --> 00:02:26.673
It was Smee who tied Wendy.

27
00:02:26.674 --> 00:02:33.060
Under his breath, he whispered, "I'll save you if you promise to be my mother."

28
00:02:33.061 --> 00:02:37.386
But this was a promise Wendy could never make to a pirate.

29
00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:46.687
The boys' eyes had drifted from Wendy to the plank, and their faces went white. They were not ready to die.

30
00:02:46.688 --> 00:02:54.900
Their walk down the narrow board and over the end into the cold sea would be the last walk they would ever take.

31
00:02:54.901 --> 00:03:00.688
They shivered and stared, no longer sure they could walk the plank as gentlemen.

32
00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:05.434
They were, after all, only little boys.

33
00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:09.126
Hook smiled and took a step toward Wendy.

34
00:03:09.127 --> 00:03:13.923
He wanted to turn her face to make her watch the boys walk the plank.

35
00:03:13.924 --> 00:03:17.635
He wanted to hear her cries of terror and regret.

36
00:03:17.636 --> 00:03:22.869
Instead, what he heard filled his own heart with terror.

37
00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:26.914
It was the tick-tock of the crocodile.

38
00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:33.265
They all heard it—Hook, the other pirates, the boys, and Wendy.

39
00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:39.354
Instantly, they all looked—but not at the water where the sound was coming from.

40
00:03:39.355 --> 00:03:42.895
All their eyes were fixed on Captain Hook.

41
00:03:42.896 --> 00:03:49.075
The crocodile, Hook knew, had only one victim in mind—him!

42
00:03:49.076 --> 00:03:53.095
He fell to the floor, trembling in a heap.

43
00:03:53.096 --> 00:03:57.869
The ticking grew louder, as if the crocodile were getting closer.

44
00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:03.400
Hook crawled on his knees to the other side of the ship, away from the boys and Wendy.

45
00:04:03.401 --> 00:04:06.560
The awful sound was getting even louder.

46
00:04:06.561 --> 00:04:12.897
All Hook could imagine was the terrible crocodile climbing aboard his ship.

47
00:04:12.898 --> 00:04:19.086
"Hide me!" Hook cried, but his men stepped back to clear the way.

48
00:04:19.087 --> 00:04:26.695
They had always been loyal to their captain, but none of them would stand between him and his fate.

49
00:04:26.696 --> 00:04:33.199
On the other side of the deck, the boys leaned over the side of the ship to see the crocodile climb in.

50
00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:38.534
But to their surprise, it was not the crocodile coming to their rescue.

51
00:04:38.535 --> 00:04:51.101
It was Peter! He made a sign for them to keep silent. Then he went on ticking.
